# What the agent image build must never see.
#
# This file exists because the build context moved. Docker reads .dockerignore
# from the context directory, so the one at the repository root stopped applying
# to this image the moment it started building from `agent/` — and the entries
# that matter in it are not about size.
#
# An agent generates its identity key on the host and keeps it in its state
# directory. Anybody who has run `CERTPILOT_AGENT_STATE=./state certpilot-agent
# enrol` while working on this module has an ed25519 private key sitting in the
# tree, and a build context is handed to the daemon whole before any instruction
# runs. A certificate management product baking its own private keys into a
# layer is the specific failure this file prevents.
.env
.env.*
.certpilot/
state/
*.pem
*.key

# Not inputs to the binary.
.git/
.github/
bin/
*.md
*.log
.DS_Store
